cases.baseline:
flexbox on the parent is usually easiest:

display: flex;
justify-content: center; /* horizontal */
align-items: center;     /* vertical */
min-height: 100vh;

If it’s just text, `text-align: center` works for horizontal. For absolute centering:

position: absolute;
top: 50%;
left: 50%;
transform: translate(-50%, -50%);

Want horizontal only or both?
